This program:
- **Warmup track** starts at t=0 and runs 5 minutes (300s) with all three athletes on the floor together.
- **Three athlete tracks** begin immediately after warmup, each following their assigned rotation across four rounds.
- **Resource constraints** enforce: one rower, one kettlebell, one box, one sled at a time; three athletes max on the floor.
- **Station sequencing** is enforced by the afterStep chain in each athlete track—no athlete can start a station until they've finished the previous one. The rotation ensures no two athletes occupy the same station simultaneously.
- **Cooldown** waits for all three athletes to finish their fourth stations, then all do 10 minutes (600s) of recovery together on the floor.

The total duration is 5 min (warmup) + 8 min per athlete (4 rounds × 2 min per station minus the final rest) + 10 min (cooldown) ≈ **45 minutes** as specified.
